  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cross-Border Assistance for Afghan Returnees</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">From January to October 2022, more than 770,000 undocumented Afghans returned from the Islamic Republic of Iran and Pakistan. This was the second-highest return total of any 10 months on record. Return trends for the 10 months of 2022 indicate that, once again, Afghanistan will exceed the Humanitarian Response Plan (HRP) estimate of 785,000 total undocumented returns in 2022, with additional expected return surges linked to a large number of Afghans leaving the country through irregular migration routes due to numerous push and pull factors. Through its cross-border return and reintegration programme, IOM is providing immediate post-arrival humanitarian assistance to vulnerable undocumented Afghan migrants and cash to cover transportation and subsistence expenses at the four IOM-supported border crossing points within the provinces of Nangarhar and Kandahar on the Pakistan border and Herat and Nimroz on the border with the Islamic Republic of Iran.</narrative>
  </description>
